tesla,2025-06,683,683,200,2400,200,2400,1,1,1,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart in its Q4-2025 (p11), Q1-2026 and Q2-2026 (p9) update decks, read from the PDFs' vector paths: at these months' scale a reading is good to a few thousand miles, and the decks disagree, end-June 2,018 / 1,473 / 245 miles, end-July 4,893 / 4,647 / 9,302 and end-August 19,697 / 19,461 / 18,481. On the Jul 23, 2025 call Elluswamy said 'We have more than seven thousand miles operating in the Austin area', a floor on the end-July cumulative that only the Q2-2026 deck's reading meets, so July's cumulative is that reading, 9,302, its band from the call's 7,000 to 15% above it; June keeps robotaxitracker's end-of-month 683 (Austin service from Jun 22), its band 200-2,400 holding the three readings; August's cumulative is the chart's ~20,000, its floor 17,900 (the lowest reading less ~3% read noise). Each month is its cumulative less the month before's, its band the difference of their bands. Austin driverless service, read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test)."
