zoox,2025-12,338181,1259920,1190013,1319873,239272,437415,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-03): the cumulative is Zoox's 'approximately 1.3 million driverless autonomous miles' at Dec 31, 2025 (letter to NHTSA, Jan 28, 2026, docket NHTSA-2025-0523-0004 p.22) less the 40,080 pre-series miles: 1,259,920. Its band, 1,190,013 to 1,319,873, is that statement's rounding (1.25M-1.35M) less the pre-series miles at their own band; later months' bands chain from it and earlier months' narrow back from it. December holds the Las Vegas growth that puts the 1M-mile crossing on about Dec 4, in the week Zoox's CTO dated it to on Dec 8, 'just last week' (Fortune, Dec 8, 2025). California's December, in no DMV report yet, is estimated from CPUC's December/November ratio (data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
zoox,2026-01,210000,1469920,1353013,1589873,163000,270000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27): Zoox's ~1.3M driverless miles at Dec 31, 2025 and 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026), read as 1.30M and 1.94M, put 640,000 miles in Jan 1-Mar 24. California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 for the DMV-reported miles CPUC misses (an assumption, the midpoint of 1.05-1.33); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, is the interval's remainder over its driving days, 6,530.74 a day. January leaves out Jan 22-26, when Las Vegas passenger service was down (LVRJ, Jan 28, 2026, dating it from an X user's posts) (data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
zoox,2026-02,230000,1699920,1537013,1876873,184000,287000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27): Zoox's ~1.3M driverless miles at Dec 31, 2025 and 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026), read as 1.30M and 1.94M, put 640,000 miles in Jan 1-Mar 24. California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 for the DMV-reported miles CPUC misses (an assumption, the midpoint of 1.05-1.33); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, is the interval's remainder over its driving days, 6,530.74 a day. January leaves out Jan 22-26, when Las Vegas passenger service was down (LVRJ, Jan 28, 2026, dating it from an X user's posts) (data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
zoox,2026-03,260000,1959920,1859918,2121276,200000,337000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27): Mar 1-24 at the Jan 1-Mar 24 rate, Mar 25-31 at the Mar 25-Aug 5 rate (as April). Cumulative band 1,859,918 to 2,121,276: 'nearly two million' read as 1.88M-2.00M as of Mar 17-24, less the pre-series miles at their own band, carried to Mar 31. It counts driverless miles: Zoox's Mar 23 post puts them 'in our robotaxi', apart from 'our retrofitted testing fleet', and with California's 1,213,646 safety-driver test miles of Dec 2024-Nov 2025 alone, a count including those would have passed 2.5M by Dec 31, 2025 (data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
zoox,2026-04,240000,2199920,2041918,2437276,182000,316000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27): 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026) and 'more than 3 million miles on public roads' (Aug 5; Bloomberg, Las Vegas Sun), read as 1.94M and 3.10M, put 1,160,000 miles in Mar 25-Aug 5, 8,656.72 a day. California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 (measured through June, then June's daily rate grown e^0.05 a month); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, 6,180.83 a day, held flat after Aug 5 (no fleet count since ~65 Las Vegas vehicles in service on Sep 2; no pause, recall or halt found). End-July cumulative floor 2,880,483: 'more than 3 million' as of Jul 29-Aug 5, less the pre-series miles' high edge; 'more than' sets no ceiling. Bands: statement rounding, drift from the window's midpoint and month noise (data/README.md, Ghost months; data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
zoox,2026-05,270000,2469920,2254918,2779276,213000,342000,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est. (rebuilt 2026-10-27): 'nearly two million autonomous miles' (Mar 23-24, 2026) and 'more than 3 million miles on public roads' (Aug 5; Bloomberg, Las Vegas Sun), read as 1.94M and 3.10M, put 1,160,000 miles in Mar 25-Aug 5, 8,656.72 a day. California is CPUC's driverless miles x 1.19 (measured through June, then June's daily rate grown e^0.05 a month); the rest, mostly Las Vegas, 6,180.83 a day, held flat after Aug 5 (no fleet count since ~65 Las Vegas vehicles in service on Sep 2; no pause, recall or halt found). End-July cumulative floor 2,880,483: 'more than 3 million' as of Jul 29-Aug 5, less the pre-series miles' high edge; 'more than' sets no ceiling. Bands: statement rounding, drift from the window's midpoint and month noise (data/README.md, Ghost months; data/README.md, Zoox anchors)."
waymo,2021-07,46137,46137,19974,63437,19974,63437,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est.: Waymo's rider-only miles by calendar year (Kusano et al. 2025, Table 2, from its Safety Impact hub: 328,000 in 2021, 524,000 in 2022) and its first million rider-only miles on Jan 21, 2023 (Waymo's one-million-mile paper), spread over the months with daily rates interpolated linearly between those totals; January 2023 keeps Jan 1-21's daily rate for the whole month. The series starts in July 2021, so the miles driven before it, 150,000 (range 150,000-260,000), come off; July-December 2021's bands and every cumulative band carry that range, and each month's band an allowance for the monthly split, half to twice a month's miles in 2022 (data/README.md, Waymo anchors; data/README.md, Waymo monthly allocation)."
