tesla,2026-04,374000,2091000,2028270,2404650,317900,467500,1,1,1,1,1,1,"Tesla's own Cumulative Paid Robotaxi Miles chart: monthly values vector-extracted from the Q2-2026 update-deck PDF (13 points through Jun-2026, 2.440M end-Q2; overlapping months re-confirm the earlier decks' series within ~8k mi). Austin + Dallas/Houston (unsupervised Dallas/Houston launch Apr 18, 2026); Bay Area remains a separate supervised series. Read as fleet service miles incl. deadhead, matching the incident scope (None + In-Vehicle + Remote Commercial/Test); if 'paid' is literally passenger-on-board miles the true total is higher, so the cumulative band's top carries ~15% upside and its floor ~3% read noise. (Pre-pin activity-ratio estimates ran ~1.4-2.9x high for Q2's months, +28% on the end-Q2 cumulative — a utilization-led slowdown the fleet counts missed.) These months' miles may include trips with a safety monitor in the driver's seat (@robotaxi on X, Sep 4, 2025: 'Safety monitors are only in the driver's seat for trips that involve highway driving'; David Moss on X, Jan 28, 2026: 'This was also my 5th ride in a row with the supervisor in the drivers [seat]'), and a crash on such a trip, if it ran as FSD (Supervised), is reportable only under NHTSA's Level 2 rules (a fatality, a hospital transport, a struck vulnerable road user, an airbag, or a tow-away of a vehicle equipped with an ADS) and goes to its Level 2 file, whose Tesla reports this page does not count: a possible pro-Tesla bias of unknown size that the no-monitor line avoids (data/README.md, Tesla's no-monitor line)."
waymo,2026-04,18025220,240488220,238066464,243749976,16513464,19986976,1,1,1,1,1,1,"US est., bottom-up on the Waymo hub's MEASURED Q2 (Sep 24, 2026 update: 271.329M rider-only miles thru Jun-2026; re-chained 2026-09-25): CA = CPUC Q2-2026 driverless actual 9,414,525 deployment + 51,198 pilot (CPUC's total driverless VMT incl. deadhead) x 1.0576, the hub-vs-CPUC ratio for the hub's CA counties in Q2 (Q1: 1.040) = 10.01M (±3%); Maricopa 3.87M and Travis 1.72M = the hub's measured Q2 county increments (11.57M / 5.28M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); Atlanta 1.02M = the hub's measured Q2 Fulton+DeKalb increment (3.25M) split by the prior monthly shape (±10%); + rider-only metros the hub does not count (Miami, Dallas, Houston, Orlando, Nashville; San Antonio passenger service halted Apr 20 to Sep 17 after flood strandings Apr 4 and Apr 20) 1.40M [0.85M, 2.40M]. Miami/Orlando open to all Apr 15; Nashville public Apr 7. The Jun-2026 cumulative lands on the anchor: the hub's 271.329M plus 6.65M estimated in metros the hub does not count, less ~0.15M pre-series miles (data/README.md, Waymo anchors)."
